THE TIMEOUT RACE IS IN ALL THREE, SO IT DECIDES NOTHING. Two critics found it independently,
each in the arm they were reviewing:

  glm on or-nemotron: "The killer sets `timed_out` with no final `finished` re-check after the
    deadline loop, so a child completing inside the last poll window is misreported as a timeout
    and its passing output discarded -- that can flip a real Pass to Error and false-VOID a
    diagonal."

  or-nemotron on gemini: "the killer thread stores timed_out flag before sending kill signal;
    wait_with_output() returns natural exit but flag check overrides with Timeout."

I checked all three rather than taking either at face value: none re-checks `finished` before
declaring a timeout. The base had no timeout reporting at all -- row 6 of my table asked for it
and never mentioned the race between a process finishing and the deadline firing. N-of-N, mine,
filed. Vetoed as a differentiator.

Worth recording that glm reported this against or-nemotron while sharing it, and did not say so.
On cell-record it disclosed the same kind of overlap unprompted; here it did not.

